-- title:
--   Germs at a point below both branches lie in both prolongations
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundled model datum for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\mathbb Z$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$, and let $\iota_K \colon K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O$ for the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, assumed integral, and let $x$ be a point of $X_O$. Let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from the function field of $X_O$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot p$, subject to two normalisations: for every $a \in O$ the germ at $x$ of the corresponding global section of $X_O$ is sent by $\varphi$ to the constant $\iota_K(a)$, and for every element $a$ of `chartAlgFin ℤ _ (IgusaScheme.jFull p)`, the integral closure of $\mathbb Z[j]$ in the level-$p$ modular function field, the germ along the preimage of the finite chart is sent by $\varphi$ to the coefficient embedding `coeffEmb` of $a$; the preimage of the finite chart in $X_O$ is assumed nonempty. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ an algebraically closed perfect field of characteristic $p$, $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ a ring homomorphism, `data` a `ModularPolynomialData p` satisfying the Kronecker congruence, and $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality hypotheses on the two level-raising maps; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data at level $N = 1$ and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple` over $P$, with its two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`. Assume $\iota_K$ carries $O$ into $A$ and that $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to k$ is the composite of this with $\mathrm{red}$. Assume finally that the images of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$, each followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, both specialise to $x$. Then for every germ $s$ in the stalk of $X_O$ at $x$, the image of $s$ in the function field lies, under $\varphi$, simultaneously in the valuation ring $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation ring $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$.
--
--   This is the orientation-free branch identification for the Deligne–Rapoport model: a point of the arithmetic surface to which the generic points of both components of the geometric special fibre specialise has its whole local ring read, through $\varphi$, into both Gauss-type prolongations of the place $A$. It is used in the node-integrality statement [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_nodeIntegers_of_stalk_of_specializes_of_exists_sub_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_nodeIntegers_of_stalk_of_specializes_of_exists_sub_mem), and rests on the dichotomy results `not_isClosed_of_forall_stalk_mem_integersFst` and `not_isClosed_of_forall_stalk_mem_integersSnd` together with the classification of points over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$.
